WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.460
Start SpecWithCode with a project, a coordinator and two workers.

2
00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:11.741
This run uses SpecWithCode 1.0.45.

3
00:00:11.741 --> 00:00:15.990
Settings, General, About shows the version on your Mac.

4
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.407
Click the plus next to Projects.

5
00:00:18.407 --> 00:00:23.949
New project starts one from a name. Local folder adopts a repo you already have.

6
00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:28.695
Here it's greet-app, with SpecWeave and one increment of two tasks.

7
00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.100
The project opens on its coordinator.

8
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.416
Choose Full access for this demo.

9
00:00:33.416 --> 00:00:36.122
It applies to every chat in this project.

10
00:00:36.122 --> 00:00:39.472
Then ask the coordinator for a two-part change:

11
00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:43.410
one worker per task, with titles and a short report.

12
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.358
The coordinator does none of the work itself.

13
00:00:46.358 --> 00:00:48.220
It starts two worker threads,

14
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.034
and they appear in the right panel under Working.

15
00:00:51.034 --> 00:00:56.663
Each one gets a brief: claim, implement, test, close and report.

16
00:00:56.663 --> 00:01:01.021
The workers share one checkout, so each works on its own files.

17
00:01:01.021 --> 00:01:04.135
Each plan chip counts the increment's tasks done,

18
00:01:04.135 --> 00:01:06.037
from zero to two of two.

19
00:01:06.037 --> 00:01:09.320
The whole run took under a minute; it's sped up here.

20
00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:13.186
Open a worker. Its result stays in its own thread.

21
00:01:13.186 --> 00:01:17.132
Its first message is the coordinator's brief, with your words.

22
00:01:17.132 --> 00:01:21.019
A final message with three headed sections becomes a report card,

23
00:01:21.019 --> 00:01:23.546
saved in the increment's reports folder.

24
00:01:23.546 --> 00:01:25.790
Open report reads it in full.

25
00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.920
Click the plan chip: both tasks are done,

26
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.438
and both acceptance criteria are met.

27
00:01:31.438 --> 00:01:34.684
Open spec and Open increment go to its files.

28
00:01:34.684 --> 00:01:39.200
This chip matched increment 0001 by the thread's title,

29
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.100
so put the increment number in each worker's title.

30
00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.990
Next: keep working when a provider runs out.
